This my my InternalTeamGroup model method:

``` php
 public function getGroupsByDomainId() {
  $result = $this->find('all', array(
   'contain' => array(
    'InternalTeamMember' => array(
     'conditions' => array(
      'active' => true
     )
    ),
    'InternalTeamMember.InternalMemberImage',
    'Domain'
   ),
   'conditions' => array(
    $this->alias . '.' . 'active' => 1,
    $this->alias . '.' . 'domain_id' => $this->domainData('id'),
   ),
   'order' => $this->alias . '.' . 'sort_order ASC',
  ));

  return $result;
 }
```

This is the association to the image model inside my InternalTeamMember.php

``` php
 public $belongsTo = array(
  'InternalMemberImage' => array(
   'className' => 'FileStorage.ImageStorage',
   'foreignKey' => 'image_name',
   'table' => 'wa_file_storage'
  )
 );
```

If you check the file storage model you see it is setting Model::$tableName but NOT prefix. I've tried to debug this in the cores model class and my guess is that something related to the way all these checks around the tableName and tablePrefix are not building the right prefix anymore.
